      "content": "KINGS LANGLEY          \tHIGH STREET TL 0702 \t\t\t\t\t(West side)                                        13/150                                  \tNos. 46, 48, and 50 - GV                                      \tII Block of 3 houses. C18, or earlier building refronted ('IK 1762' cut in brick on front of No. 46). No. 50 C19. Said to be timber framed. Red brick front and S end, tilehung S gable, old red tile steep roof. Originally a pair of 16 storeys and cellar houses facing E, with 3 windows, 2 doors, shared central chimney, and 3 gabled dormers at the eaves. S extension (No. 50) of same height and matching materials has an external S gable chimney, a matching dormer and a small-paned casement window adjoining the doorpost. The 3-light casement windows of the older part have segmental arches and external shutters. 4-panel flush beaded doors alternate. Segmental arch to central cellar windows. Listing NGR: TL0721302586"
    }
